The second run got farther—`lake clean` passed—but Lean itself cannot resolve `/proc/<pid>/exe` in this audit container because the process PID namespace and mounted `/proc` disagree. I found the exact failure mechanism (`$$` is PID 2 while `/proc/2` is absent). I’m applying a narrow read-only compatibility shim that redirects only missing `/proc/<pid>/exe` lookups to `/proc/self/exe`, then rerunning the unchanged trusted preflight.
